# A merge and a method of the unit that form their inputs alike reach one
# formal handed on, and one formation serves both. five and g1 each read
# the one name other, a field of the unit, 9. take calls its formal; mid
# hands its own formal to take. The root gives mid g1: 10. passed gives mid
# merge(y: 5; five): 14. under has other 20: 25 and 21. Entry 7.
int: other 9

fn: five (int: y) int
    return: y + other

fn: g1 () int
    return: other + 1
end: g1

fn: take (g1: op) int
    return: op()
end: take

fn: mid (g1: p) int
    return: take(p)
end: mid

fn: passed () int
    return: mid: merge(y: 5; five)
end: passed

fn: under () int
    int: other 20
    return: passed() * 100 + mid(g1)
end: under

int: a mid(g1)
int: d passed()
int: e under()
int: ok 7
if: a != 10 || d != 14 || e != 2521
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
